## Shadow lightweight live image
##
## Kali Linux + Xfce + LightDM + Picom + NetworkManager + Bluetooth + PipeWire
## + ZRAM + Firefox + essential desktop applications + Live boot.
##
## Philosophy: install useful software, do NOT auto-start normal applications,
## do NOT remove optional services that can be re-enabled later, and keep the
## big kali-tools-* collections OUT.
##
## $ ./build.sh --variant shadow

## Base Kali system + live-boot / live-config (required for live boot)
kali-linux-core
kali-desktop-live

## Lightweight XFCE desktop. This metapackage pulls Xfce core (xfce4, session,
## panel, settings, xfconf, xfdesktop4, xfwm4, appfinder), QTerminal, Thunar,
## Parole, Atril, Ristretto, Engrampa, xfce4-screenshooter, PipeWire audio,
## LightDM, pavucontrol and more — all listed explicitly below where we
## depend on them directly.
kali-desktop-xfce

## Display manager (auto-login for the shadow user, see common lightdm.conf)
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter

## Shell + terminal (QTerminal — installed, NOT auto-started)
zsh
qterminal

## Compositor — lightweight config at /etc/xdg/picom.conf, auto-started at
## login via /etc/xdg/autostart/picom.desktop (see includes.chroot)
picom

## Fonts: Fira Code default for normal/bold text, Cantarell for UI, URW
## base35 fallback. fonts-dejavu-core guarantees the ☯ prompt glyph (U+262F)
## and its box-drawing glyphs. Noto Egyptian Hieroglyphs (extracted from
## fonts-noto-core by hooks/live/install-noto-glyphs.chroot, package then
## discarded) is fallback-only for Egyptian glyphs.
fonts-firacode
fonts-urw-base35
fonts-mathjax
fonts-cantarell
fonts-dejavu-core
xfonts-utils
xfonts-encodings

## Thunar file manager extras - volume management, drive/USB auto-mount.
## Thunar is installed and available but never auto-opens at boot.
## (thunar + nm-connection-editor are also hard Depends of kali-desktop-xfce /
##  network-manager-applet respectively; listed explicitly per spec §5/§7.)
thunar
thunar-volman
thunar-archive-plugin
gvfs
gvfs-backends
udisks2

## Networking - NetworkManager (with nm-applet tray icon), WPA supplicant and
## rfkill control. NetworkManager must start automatically (essential desktop
## function); the applet lives in the Xfce panel.
network-manager
network-manager-applet
nm-connection-editor
wpasupplicant
rfkill

## Bluetooth - service stays ENABLED (bluetooth.service is NOT disabled/masked,
## see hooks/live/optimize-services.chroot). Blueman gives a tray applet and
## device pairing; pairing headsets/speakers/keyboards works right after login.
bluez
blueman

## Audio - modern lightweight PipeWire stack. Services auto-start; the
## pavucontrol GUI is installed but does NOT open at boot.
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
pavucontrol

## Web browser - installed, NOT auto-started
firefox-esr

## Desktop applications - installed, NOT auto-started. Parole/Atril/Ristretto/
## Engrampa/xfce4-screenshooter are already Depends of kali-desktop-xfce;
## listed here explicitly so the intent is visible and the selection does not
## silently shrink if the metapackage changes.
parole
atril
ristretto
engrampa
xfce4-screenshooter
baobab
gparted

## Polkit daemon (desktop privilege handling)
polkitd

## zram swap for low-RAM hardware (auto-started)
systemd-zram-generator

## Optional services kept AVAILABLE but DISABLED at boot (see
## hooks/live/optimize-services.chroot): printing (CUPS), mDNS/Avahi, mobile
## broadband (ModemManager), PackageKit. Re-enable later with:
##   sudo systemctl enable --now <unit>
avahi-daemon
cups
modemmanager
packagekit

## No kali-tools-* / security-tool metapackages on purpose. This is a light
## desktop, not a preloaded pentest toolkit; tools are installed individually
## when needed.